ImapGoose is a daemon that keeps local maildir-format directories in
sync with a mail server over IMAP. It is similar to OfflineIMAP, but
relies on the modern IMAP extensions to efficiently keep everything
synchronized without the need for periodic polling.

It implements the same general synchronisation algorithm as OfflineIMAP [0].
And also listens to NOTIFY events for real-time server notifications of changes.

Features:

- Bidirectional synchronisation using the same algorithm as offlineimap.
- Automatic mailbox discovery: synchronises all mailboxes on the server.
- Real-time updates using IMAP NOTIFY for instant email synchronisation.
- Daemon mode for continuous synchronisation.
- Concurrent syncing of multiple accounts and all mailboxes.

[0] https://blog.ezyang.com/2012/08/how-offlineimap-works/
